menu "Netlab web access"

    config NETLAB_AUTH_ENABLE
        bool "Require a login for the web UI and the API"
        default y
        help
            The web page asks for a user name and password and every API route needs the
            session token it gets back ("Authorization: Bearer <token>"). The login page, the
            static files, GET /api/v1/about and, while the Wi-Fi setup network is open, the three
            Wi-Fi provisioning routes stay public: a phone joining the setup network has to be able
            to reach them. In router lab mode, POST /api/v1/router/lab (the lab service students'
            devices call) is public too; it records only while the capture is on.

            Turn it off to go back to an open API (anyone on the network can use it).

    config NETLAB_ADMIN_USER
        string "Administrator user name"
        default "admin"
        depends on NETLAB_AUTH_ENABLE

    config NETLAB_ADMIN_PASSWORD
        string "Administrator password (LAB ONLY, plain text)"
        default "admin"
        depends on NETLAB_AUTH_ENABLE
        help
            LAB ONLY. This value is compiled into the firmware and written in clear text to
            sdkconfig, and this repository is public, so the default is known to everyone. The web
            UI is plain HTTP, so the browser also sends it in clear over the network at each login.
            That is acceptable on a home network you control; do not expose the device to the
            internet. Set your own value in menuconfig: it lands in sdkconfig, which git ignores.

    config NETLAB_SESSION_TTL_MIN
        int "Session lifetime without use (minutes)"
        default 30
        range 1 1440
        depends on NETLAB_AUTH_ENABLE
        help
            Each request extends the session, so it only ends after this long without any.
            Up to four sessions live at once (a phone and a PC); a fifth login replaces the one
            that would expire first.

endmenu
